{"id":"n5-057","title":"Verb ること～","romaji":"〜ru koto","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Express an action or event as a noun; 'the act of', 'doing'.","longExplanation":"The ること grammar point is used to nominalize or turn a verb into a noun, which represents the action or event itself as a concept. It can be translated as 'the act of' or simply 'doing' in English. This formation is used with verbs in the dictionary (ru-)form.","formation":"Verb (dictionary form) + こと","examples":[{"jp":"泳ぐことが大好きです。","romaji":"Oyogu koto ga daisuki desu.","en":"I love swimming.","words":[{"surface":"泳ぐ","vocabId":"1174340","reading":"およぐ"},{"surface":"こと","vocabId":"1313580","reading":"こと"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"大好き","vocabId":"1413660","reading":"だいすき"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[1]},{"jp":"日本語を勉強することは楽しいです。","romaji":"Nihongo wo benkyou suru koto wa tanoshii desu.","en":"Studying Japanese is fun.","words":[{"surface":"日本語","vocabId":"1464530","reading":"にほんご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"する","vocabId":"1595910","reading":"する"},{"surface":"こと","vocabId":"1313580","reading":"こと"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"楽しい","vocabId":"1207240","reading":"たのしい"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"友達と話すことがストレスを軽減します。","romaji":"Tomodachi to hanasu koto ga sutoresu wo keigen shimasu.","en":"Talking with friends reduces stress.","words":[{"surface":"友達","vocabId":"1540170","reading":"ともだち"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話す","vocabId":"1562350","reading":"はなす"},{"surface":"こと","vocabId":"1313580","reading":"こと"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ストレス","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"軽減","vocabId":"1252680","reading":"けいげん"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface